{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And they journeyed, and there was, etc.</b> Perhaps it intends to convey a novel point: that although they departed from there — and this would indicate an aspect of flight — nevertheless, ״וַיְהִי חִתַּת״ etc. Or in this manner: although they saw that they had escaped from their hand and gone on their way, nevertheless a terror fell upon them and they did not pursue, and they consented to their escape."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:05.587151946Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}